### 1. TanStack Query (React Query) — Server State
TanStack Query handles all the hard parts of server state: caching, background refetching, stale-while-revalidate, optimistic updates, and pagination.
```jsx
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['users', userId],
  queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`).then(r => r.json()),
  staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
});
```

### 2. Zustand — Minimal Global State
Zustand uses a simple hook-based API without boilerplate:
```jsx
const useStore = create((set) => ({
  user: null,
  setUser: (user) => set({ user }),
  logout: () => set({ user: null }),
}));
```

### 3. React Hook Form — Performant Forms
RHF uses uncontrolled inputs by default — avoids re-rendering on every keystroke. Integrates with Zod for schema validation.

